member.summary:
Emits a value from  only if it has not been seen before, anywhere in the stream
since subscription — using  (or the default equality comparer for
).

Terminates the subject with an error: forwards it to every observer currently subscribed, marks the subject
as stopped, and clears the observer list (any late subscriber will immediately receive the same error — see
). A no-op once the subject has already stopped or been disposed.

Executes queued actions due at or before , in due-time/scheduling-order, until
none remain (an action may itself schedule more work for the same drain pass — e.g. an operator's
internal recursive timer chain — and that new work is picked up too, as long as it is still due within
). Does not itself move  past the last action it actually ran;
callers that need the clock to land exactly on a target value () do that themselves.
